 active: re-reading `hook-wiring-check.cjs:264-269` confirms that `NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN.has(flag)` tests the whole token, so `--eval=0`, `-e\"1\"` and `-p\"1\"` never match, and the marker is then accepted as node's script word. The counterevidence searched is unchanged: no later re-test of the marker as an argument, and no test covers the attached spelling. Final severity stays P1 because the check's stated contract is to read the command the way a shell runs it, and the caller at `doctor-setup.yaml:61` turns the false `ok claude` into a PASS delivery leg.\n29-\n30-### P2 Findings\n31-\n32-None.\n33-\n34-## Traceability Checks\n35-\n36-| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n37-|----------|--------|----------|\n38-| `spec_code` | pass | The caller surface matches the changed behavior: both doctor routes read the check's printed lines and its exit codes, and neither parses the internal flag tables. |\n39-| `checklist_evidence` | partial | CHK-FIX-005's matrix covers the space-separated forms only, which is the exact gap the carried P1 names; no checklist row claims the attached form. |\n40-| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | Closed in iteration 3. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"DR3-P1-001\\\" -A 12 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/doctor-docs-3/iterations/iteration-004.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794595391161,"end":1794595392506}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794595392512,"sessionID":"ses_e29ccdea6ffe1z7wL2sWcEOG4A","part":{"partID":"prt_1d638895b001WB3rtyTIQxdijM","sessionID":"ses_e29ccdea6ffe1z7wL2sWcEOG4A","messageID":"msg_1d638790d00191RJnjcqqJXqkg","type":"tool","id":"call_4eca3de4ee9347d98ada92ad","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"AR3-P2-001\" -A 12 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/advisor-runtime-3/iterations/iteration-004.md | head -40"},"output":"42:| `spec_code` | pass | Task-line conformance table below; every changed production file maps to a task line and the code does what the line says, with the one wording exception already recorded as AR3-P2-001 in iteration 1. |\n43-| `checklist_evidence` | pass | Changed tests actually fail when their fix is removed: T045's owner assertion would change the label to `system-spec-kit → ...`; T027's label includes the policy; T028 asserts the three fields on the CLI path; T006 asserts the stored marker exists and the status text does not carry it; T007 deletes an assertion that never reached a gate. |\n44-| `skill_agent` | pass | The plugin removal has no reader: `parseCliResponse` metadata consumers use `freshness` only (`system-skill-advisor.js:1522`), and no runtime file reads `metadata.compiledRouteSummary`. |\n45-| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | No agent file in this area. |\n46-| `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | Catalog pages naming `metadata.compiledRouteSummary` belong to other skills and are one of the four items the task block excludes from this pass. |\n47-| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | Playbook files belong to the `doctor-docs` area. |\n48-\n49-### Task-line conformance\n50-\n51-| Task | Files | Verdict |\n52-|------|-------|---------|\n53:| T003 shared no-edit helper | `command-attach.ts`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | 