est.ts` | Holds: `delete env.AI_SESSION_CHILD`, hook sees `<unset>`. |\n--\n72:| T042 narrow the no-edit pattern | `command-attach.ts`, tests | Partial: the three named cases hold, the `make no changes` variant still misfires (AR3-P2-001). |\n73-| T043 end the `--row-id` sentence | `routing-accuracy/README.md` | `doctor-docs` area file; out of this lineage. |\n74-\n75-## Integration Evidence\n76-\n77-- The removed plugin metadata field has no consumer: `grep` over `.opencode` and the advisor runtime shows only the test-local fixture builder and `lib/skill-advisor-render.js` helpers, both of which serve the separate compiled-route renderer, not the plugin metadata.\n78-- The status printer still reports `bounded_compiled_route_summary=${options.boundedCompiledRouteSummary}` at `system-skill-advisor.js:1684`, which is what the corrected jsdoc names.\n79-- The plugin test's row now sets `skillId: 'system-spec-kit'` with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'` (T045), so dropping the owner changes the rendered label.\n80-\n81-## Edge Cases\n82-\n83-- `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` stays exported while `isNoEditRequest` is the safe entry. No production caller reads the raw pattern; the test at `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:49` keeps it alive for the legacy assertion. Recorded as a design edge; a future caller could bypass the fold, but no concrete current input does.\n84-- The four catalog pages naming `metadata.compiledRouteSummary` are explicitly left by the task block's \"Verifier follow-ups, coordinator\" note, so they are not re-reported here.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"42:| `spec_code` | pass | Task-line conformance table below; every changed production file maps to a task line and the code does what the line says, with the one wording exception already recorded as AR3-P2-001 in iteration 1. |\n43-| `checklist_evidence` | pass | Changed tests actually fail when their fix is removed: T045's ow