{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794595642322,"sessionID":"ses_e29ccdea6ffe1z7wL2sWcEOG4A","part":{"partID":"prt_1d63c59100026QEn6bnKY1C0x3","sessionID":"ses_e29ccdea6ffe1z7wL2sWcEOG4A","messageID":"msg_1d63c449a001oyl24tJ0PtNTnR","type":"tool","id":"call_70eb6054114746e5a590278f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"hook-wiring-check\" .skilled/commands/doctor --include=*.yaml --include=*.md --include=*.cjs | grep -v tests | head"},"output":".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:30:  'Usage: hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <dir> [--json]',\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:75:  process.stderr.write(`hook-wiring-check: ${message}\\n`);\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:352:    process.stderr.write(`hook-wiring-check: ${err && err.message ? err.message : String(err)}\\n`);\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:40:  hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:61:    - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37:  hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60:    - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:30:  'Usage: hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <dir> [--json]',\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:75:  process.stderr.write(`hook-wiring-check: ${message}\\n`);\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:352:    process.stderr.write(`hook-wiring-check: ${err && err.message ? err.message : String(err)}\\n`);\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:40:  hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:61:    - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37:  hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60:    - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"hook-wiring-check\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor --include=*.yaml --include=*.md --include=*.cjs | grep -v tests | head\"}"},"time":{"start":1794595641616,"end":1794595642322}}}}
