{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794595683069,"sessionID":"ses_e29ccdea6ffe1z7wL2sWcEOG4A","part":{"partID":"prt_1d63cf1da0024Dqwpi6XFLiU9F","sessionID":"ses_e29ccdea6ffe1z7wL2sWcEOG4A","messageID":"msg_1d63ce331001gOBr6aK5kDhW9O","type":"tool","id":"call_bccd433e31a94fed80193837","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"The short form is caught (`node -e\"1\" <marker>` reaches the test as `-e1` and prints `hook-missing`), while the long form is not: `node --check\"1\" <marker>` also prints `ok claude` (exit 0) although node refuses `--check1`. This window predates the commit (the old set membership missed `--eval1` the same way); it is reported because the commit's own claim is that a flag carrying its value in the same word is now read by name, and the quote-merged long form is that class.","oldString":"The short form is caught (`node -e\"1\" <marker>` reaches the test as `-e1` and prints `hook-missing`), and so is `node --check\"1\"`? no -- `node --check\"1\" <marker>` also prints `ok claude` (exit 0) while node refuses `--check1`. This window predates the commit (the old set membership missed `--eval1` the same way); it is reported because the commit's own claim is that a flag carrying its value in the same word is now read by name, and the quote-merged long form is that class.","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md\n@@ -27,9 +27,9 @@\n None. The reported defect is closed for every attached spelling it names, and no working command among the ten forms run is misread.\n \n ### P2 Findings\n \n-1. **A long flag whose value is attached by shell quoting still reports `ok` for a command node refuses to run** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:232` -- The name split only handles `=`. `readWords` merges a quoted value into the same word, so `node --eval\"1\" <marker>` reaches the flag test as `--eval1`, which is not in `NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN` and is then skipped as an unknown long flag; the marker becomes the script word and the check prints `ok claude`. Node itself refuses the same command with `bad option: --eval1` (exit 9), so the hook cannot run while the check reports it wired. The short form is caught (`node -e\"1\" <marker>` reaches the test as `-e1` and prints `hook-missing`), and so is `node --check\"1\"`? no -- `node --check\"1\" <marker>` also prints `ok claude` (exit 0) while node refuses `--check1`. This window predates the commit (the old set membership missed `--eval1` the same way); it is reported because the commit's own claim is that a flag carrying its value in the same word is now read by name, and the quote-merged long form is that class.\n+1. **A long flag whose value is attached by shell quoting still reports `ok` for a command node refuses to run** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:232` -- The name split only handles `=`. `readWords` merges a quoted value into the same word, so `node --eval\"1\" <marker>` reaches the flag test as `--eval1`, which is not in `NODE_FLAGS_WITHOUT_RUN` and is then skipped as an unknown long flag; the marker becomes the script word and the check prints `ok claude`. Node itself refuses the same command with `bad option: --eval1` (exit 9), so the hook cannot run while the check reports it wired. The short form is caught (`node -e\"1\" <marker>` reaches the test as `-e1` and prints `hook-missing`), while the long form is not: `node --check\"1\" <marker>` also prints `ok claude` (exit 0) although node refuses `--check1`. This window predates the commit (the old set membership missed `--eval1` the same way); it is reported because the commit's own claim is that a flag carrying its value in the same word is now read by name, and the quote-merged long form is that class.\n    Finding class: class-of-bug (residual window of the class the commit narrows).\n    Scope proof: the name split is on the changed line `hook-wiring-check.cjs:232`; `readWords:133-147` merges a quoted value into the flag word, which is what produces `--eval1`.\n    Affected surface hints: `doctor-setup.yaml:61` delivery leg (exit 0 is PASS), `doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60` (exit 0 leaves the status unchanged).\n    Case: fixture `.claude/settings.json` with `node --eval\"1\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` -> `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <fixture>` printed `ok claude` and exited 0, while `node --eval\"1\"` itself exits 9 with `bad option: --eval1`.\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"The short form is caught (`node -e\\\"1\\\" <marker>` reaches the test as `-e1` and prints `hook-missing`), while the long form is not: `node --check\\\"1\\\" <marker>` also prints `ok claude` (exit 0) although node refuses `--check1`. This window predates the commit (the old set membership missed `--eval1` the same way); it is reported because the commit's own claim is that a flag carrying its value in the same word is now read by name, and the quote-merged long form is that class.\",\"oldString\":\"The short form is caught (`node -e\\\"1\\\" <marker>` reaches the test as `-e1` and prints `hook-missing`), and so is `node --check\\\"1\\\"`? no -- `node --check\\\"1\\\" <marker>` also prints `ok claude` (exit 0) while node refuses `--check1`. This window predates the commit (the old set membership missed `--eval1` the same way); it is reported because the commit's own claim is that a flag carrying its value in the same word is now read by name, and the quote-merged long form is that class.\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794595680730,"end":1794595683069}}}}
