{"type":"text","timestamp":1794596048095,"sessionID":"ses_e29ccdea6ffe1z7wL2sWcEOG4A","part":{"id":"prt_1d6427da00012cq35LOTQi68Bh","sessionID":"ses_e29ccdea6ffe1z7wL2sWcEOG4A","messageID":"msg_1d6426e02001jp37tbc64Fki23","type":"text","text":"Lineage `noedit-confirm-3b` complete. Verdict **CONDITIONAL** (P0 0, P1 1, P2 2), stop reason `maxIterationsReached` at iteration 3 of 3.\n\n- **No-edit fix does not fully hold — it introduced a regression (P1 `NE3-P1-001`)**: `command-attach.ts:289` now reads `make no changes to the tests` as a change request (`isNoEditRequest` false, `attachCommand` returns `/create:agent`), where the bare `make no changes` still returns true. A second gap (P2 `NE3-P2-002`): the guard only matches one literal space, so newline, tab, two-space, colon and comma variants still lose the command exactly as the pass-three finding described.\n- **Hook check fix holds with no new defect**: `node -e1`, `node --eval=1`, `node --print=1`, `node --check=1`, `node -p1` all print `hook-missing` exit 1; ten plausible working forms print `ok claude` exit 0. One exotic window predates the commit (P2 `NE3-P2-003`: `node --eval\"1\" <marker>` still prints `ok` while node exits 9).\n- Evidence: both single test files run (26 and 32 passed), 17 check fixtures executed under the lineage directory, holdout proven untouched by counts/numstat only.\n\nArtifacts in `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-confirm-3b`: 3 iterations, 3 deltas, gateway-recorded state (5 ledger-backed rows), refreshed registry/dashboard, and `review-report.md` with the Planning Packet.\n\nFANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:noedit-confirm-3b","time":{"start":1794596044192,"end":1794596048095}}}
